          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "atmosphere, water or life on the Moon, these features stay on the Moon’s surface for a very long time."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 1,
          "bbox": [
            0.115,
            0.135,
            0.744,
            0.218
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Although the Moon is very far, humans have sent spacecrafts to explore and understand more about the Moon. India has also launched three Chandrayaan missions to study the Moon, and a further mission is being planned."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 2,
          "bbox": [
            0.156,
            0.271,
            0.85,
            0.374
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "To improve our understanding of the Moon, India’s first mission to the Moon, Chandrayaan-1, was launched in 2008 and the second mission, Chandrayaan-2, in 2019. The third mission, Chandrayaan-3, was launched in July 2023 and its Vikram lander carrying the Pragyan rover successfully soft-landed on the Moon on 23 August 2023. With"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
            0.126,
            0.399,
            0.195,
            0.449
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "image_body",
              "index": 3,
              "bbox": [
                0.126,
                0.399,
                0.195,
                0.449
              ],
              "image_path": "images/page_14_image_3.jpg",
              "content": ""
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.115,
            0.455,
            0.205,
            0.497
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Do you know?",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.22,
            0.374,
            0.825,
            0.498
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "this mission, India became the first country in the world to achieve a landing near the little explored Moon’s south pole. To mark this success, the Government of India declared 23 August to be celebrated as ‘National Space Day’ in India. A fourth mission, Chandrayaan-4, is being planned which aims to bring back soil and rock samples from the Moon."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.116,
            0.535,
            0.234,
            0.556
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Asteroids"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.114,
            0.568,
            0.746,
            0.65
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "The Sun and the planets are nearly spherical in shape. There are many small objects in the Solar System which are rocky and irregular in shape. These are called asteroids. Many of these asteroids revolve around the Sun in paths that"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.115,
            0.65,
            0.54,
            0.733
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "lie between those of Mars and Jupiter. This region is called the asteroid belt (Fig. 12.7). Occasionally, some asteroids pass very close to the Earth."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 9,
          "bbox": [
            0.117,
            0.739,
            0.212,
            0.76
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Comets"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 10,
          "bbox": [
            0.583,
            0.675,
            0.729,
            0.757
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "The sizes of asteroids are from 10 m to about 500 km."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "index": 11,
          "bbox": [
            0.784,
            0.655,
            0.853,
            0.706
          ],
          "content": [
